    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "3 BEDROOM PLUS ATTIC CONVERSION/ 3 BATHROOM\r\n\r\nDixon Residential Estate Agents are delighted to present 53 Palmer Court to the Rush property market.\r\n\r\nNo. 53 Palmer Court is presented in excellent condition and offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation extending to approximately 98.8 sq.m. (1063 sq.ft.). The ground floor comprises a welcoming entrance hallway leading to a spacious living room, with double doors opening into a modern open-plan kitchen and dining area overlooking the rear garden. Upstairs, the first floor offers three well-appointed bedrooms, including a generous principal bedroom complete with en-suite, together with a contemporary family bathroom. A converted attic provides an excellent additional space, ideal for use as a home office, playroom, gym or guest accommodation, offering valuable flexibility to suit a variety of lifestyles.\r\n\r\nFor families, Rush provides a range of schooling options. The village has several well-regarded primary and secondary schools. Rush National School and St. Catherine's National School are among the primary schools, both offering strong academic programs and extracurricular activities. For older children, St. Joseph's Secondary School serves the area and is known for its diverse curriculum. Nearby towns like Skerries and Lusk also have additional educational facilities, easily accessible to residents of Rush. In terms of transportation, Rush is well-connected to Dublin city and the surrounding areas. The village benefits from good public transport links, including regular bus services that travel to Dublin city centre and other nearby towns. The Rush and Lusk train station, located just outside the village, provides direct access to Dublin via the commuter rail service, making it convenient for those who work in the city. The village is also within easy reach of the M1 motorway, allowing for quick access to Dublin Airport and other major routes. For those who prefer driving, the road network provides smooth connectivity to both rural and urban areas, making commuting relatively hassle-free.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is strongly advised.\r\n\r\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***"
